UID:27livmr210418p9ru8grag9n4i@google.com
CREATED:20260128T000839Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Legacy 1000 KTES shows AC not supervised in alarm.  Will the
  below resolve this?</p><p><br></p><p>Need to check and let me know what pl
 anning we need to do.</p><p>Currently\, both doors unlock at the same time 
 for a defined set of time and then relock together at the end of the time c
 ycle.</p><p> </p><p>We will functionally separate the doors into Exterior a
 nd Interior which will allow for:</p><ul> <li>The exterior door will unlock
      for up to 10 seconds\, and it will relock once the door closes – so th
 ose     moving quickly will have a secure door behind them.</li> <li>The in
 terior door will unlock     for 15 seconds\, allowing time to get to the in
 terior door and move     through. This door will stay unlocked for the full
  15 seconds rather than     lock when closed (to avoid issues with someone 
 leaving at the time and the     door locking prematurely). </li></ul><p> </
 p><p>If someone doesn’t get to the second door in time\, they can use a new
  reader in the vestibule to open the interior door.</p><p>If someone uses t
 he reader in the vestibule\, it will ONLY unlock the interior door. This en
 hances safety of someone who is waiting in or entered the vestibule and the
 re is a threat outside the main doors\, they can safely move back into the 
 building without unlocking the exterior door.</p><p> </p><p>We will continu
 e the convenience function of swiping at the exterior to unlock both doors 
 to travel through. The same will occur with the Intercom – as it does now.<
 /p><p> </p><p>Since 5 elevator cab controls were planned for and never adde
 d\, there are sufficient free door slots on the controller’s available onsi
 te to facilitate this work. </p><p>We will rewire and relocate one single d
 oor controller from the Parkade up to the 2000 Office to facilitate 2000’s 
 separation.</p><p>In 1000 and 3000\, additional cabling will be required to
  be run from the main entrance to the parkade mechanical rooms below. </p><
