 d for the recorder itself is Vista1234\nOur oldnotes said we also set the v
 erification code: Vista1234\n \nJust forreference I told the previous manag
 ement before there is a Hik connect account\nYou couldgive the details to t
 he other company. And that way\, they can login into theaccount.\n \nForref
 erence\nhttps://www.hik-connect.com/views/terms/newHelp/helpIos/GUID-F99ECC
 1B-E529-416A-9093-46A33500D60C.html\nThis linksaid if you want to unbind vi
 a the hik connect account\, Make sure thedevice and the phone running the M
 obile Client are in the same local areanetwork. (Meaning the person doing i
 t has to be there in person).\n \nWe sentthis to the previous management:\n
 Notesfor account on the Hik Connect app.The Bella Vista camera recorder vie
 wing was shared tothis account. \nIt can begiven to the board\, and they ca
 n sharethe account information with the intended people. \nThey can useit t
 o view the camera system. \nThis isfaster than setting up sharing for multi
 ple accounts for multiple people.\n \nThis information was used to make an 
 account onthe Hik Connect app.\nemail: bellavistacameraapp@gmail.com (mailt
 o:bellavistacameraapp@gmail.com)\npassword: Be7563@!C\nThe information is a
 lso used fora Gmail account. It uses the same password.\nReceived this\, as
 well.\n \nThe technicianmentioned to me that while he is onsite today\, he 
 should be able to unbind theHik connect account.\n \nFor reference\,we didn
 't put that on our technician's account login\, we made the one newaccount\
 , which the management and the board could use for remote viewing. \n \nPle
 ase note\,when that account is disconnected it won't have remote viewing ac
 cess\, unlesssomeone sets it up to have remote viewing again. \n\nRoman Kus
