CREATED:20260507T200336Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Legacy 1000 KTES shows AC not supervised in alarm.  Will the
  below resolve this?</p><p>Need to check and let me know what planning we n
 eed to do.</p><p>Currently\, both doors unlock at the same time for a defin
 ed set of time and then relock together at the end of the time cycle.</p><p
 >We will functionally separate the doors into Exterior and Interior which w
 ill allow for:</p><ul> <li>The exterior door will unlock     for up to 10 s
 econds\, and it will relock once the door closes – so those     moving quic
 kly will have a secure door behind them.</li> <li>The interior door will un
 lock     for 15 seconds\, allowing time to get to the interior door and mov
 e     through. This door will stay unlocked for the full 15 seconds rather 
 than     lock when closed (to avoid issues with someone leaving at the time
  and the     door locking prematurely). </li></ul><p>If someone doesn’t get
  to the second door in time\, they can use a new reader in the vestibule to
  open the interior door.</p><p>If someone uses the reader in the vestibule\
 , it will ONLY unlock the interior door. This enhances safety of someone wh
 o is waiting in or entered the vestibule and there is a threat outside the 
 main doors\, they can safely move back into the building without unlocking 
 the exterior door.</p><p>We will continue the convenience function of swipi
 ng at the exterior to unlock both doors to travel through. The same will oc
 cur with the Intercom – as it does now.</p><p> </p><p>Since 5 elevator cab 
 controls were planned for and never added\, there are sufficient free door 
 slots on the controller’s available onsite to facilitate this work. </p><p>
 We will rewire and relocate one single door controller from the Parkade up 
 to the 2000 Office to facilitate 2000’s separation.</p><p>In 1000 and 3000\
 , additional cabling will be required to be run from the main entrance to t
 he parkade mechanical rooms below. </p><p>I believe that the existing cable
  tracking is full\, so a new route needs to be run alongside\, tracking is 
 used to help conceal cabling and keep it neat and is mounted on the surface
  of the wall in the lobbies and vestibule already.</p><p> </p><table> <tbod
 y><tr>  <td>  <p><b><u>Building 1000\, 2000\, 3000 - Separation of Interior
  and Exterior  Main Entrance Doors</u></b></p>  </td> </tr> <tr>  <td>  <p>
 3</p>  </td>  <td>  <p>Smart Prox Reader without Keypad</p>  </td>  <td>  <
 p>                  </p>  </td>  <td>  <p><br></p>  </td> </tr> <tr>  <td> 
  <p>3</p>  </td>  <td>  <p>Standard Installation\; at-the-door wiring\, ins
 tallation\, and  configuration</p></td><td></td><td>  </td> </tr> <tr>  <td
 >  <p>2</p>  </td>  <td>  <p>Conduit and Tracking Allowance</p></td><td></t
 d><td>  </td> </tr> <tr>  <td>  <p>1</p>  </td>  <td>  <p>Rewire and Reloca
 te Single-Door Controller\, Tracking for 2000</p></td><td></td><td>  </td> 
 </tr> <tr>  <td>  <p><br></p></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260525T181648Z
